Subject: [PATCH 10/19] Rule out OpenSky as a seed source, with measurements

Ran a pilot against February 2026 with real credentials, spending 540 of the
4,000 daily credits. It does not work, and the reason is the one bias the fit
cannot absorb.

Cost: 30 credits per call, and a two-day window costs the same as a one-day
window, so a month of all 58 airports lands near 24,000 credits, six days of
quota per month of data.

Coverage: of 9,448 departures from Mexico City that month, only 2,117 resolve
to a recognised domestic destination and 43% carry no estimated arrival
airport at all. The gaps are not even. Monterrey 92%, Tijuana 95%, Veracruz
92%, Hermosillo 94%, against 0% for Guadalajara, Merida, Puerto Vallarta,
Oaxaca and most of the map. Querying arrivals at Guadalajara and Merida
returns nothing either, so it is receiver coverage rather than a failure to
estimate the destination.

Decisive finding: resolution rates differ by carrier, 13% for Aeromexico
Connect against 37% for Viva, with Aeromexico at 26% and Volaris at 29%. The
fit absorbs a route losing flights evenly; it does not absorb one carrier
losing more of them than its rivals on the same route. A factor of nearly
three is irreducible bias.

